        "padding_bottom": 60
      }
    },
    "landscape": {
      "type": "chapter-landscape",
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/handsWeave.jpg",
        "heading": "The landscape behind the loom",
        "paragraph_1": "Maheshwar sits above the Narmada river, with its ghats and fort rising over the water. The fort’s carved stone and its river-facing walls became a pattern library for the town’s weavers, who borrowed brick, matting and flower forms for their borders.",
        "paragraph_2": "In Rajasthan, the Kota region is dry and sunlit. Cloth made here needs to be cool and airy, which is exactly what Kota Doria is: a very open weave of cotton and silk that lets air through and drapes lightly.",
        "paragraph_3": "Both traditions were supported by royal patronage, and both nearly faded when cheaper mill cloth arrived. Cooperative and design-led revivals have kept their looms running, and they are now among the most popular handloom sarees in the country.",
        "image_position_mobile": "below_text",
        "background_color": "#ffffff",
        "padding_top": 60,
        "padding_bottom": 60
      }
    },
